[{"text": "Step 4 execution complete. Integrated generateHeartbeat() into tool response handler.

CHANGES:
- Added import at top of src/mcp/server.ts: import { generateHeartbeat } from './heartbeat.js';
- Added try/catch block in registerTool success handler (after line 210)
- Calls generateHeartbeat(planDirectory) for every successful tool response
- Appends heartbeat as separate content item if it returns non-null
- Handles heartbeat failure gracefully - never breaks tool response
- Heartbeat NOT added to error responses (clean error output)

INTEGRATION POINT:
Inside registerTool handler, after result content is pushed but before return:
```typescript
// Append heartbeat footer with plan context
try {
    const heartbeat = await generateHeartbeat(planDirectory);
    if (heartbeat) {
        content.push({
            type: 'text' as const,
            text: heartbeat,
        });
    }
} catch {
    // Heartbeat failure should never break tool response
}
return { content };
```

EFFECT:
Every successful RiotPlan MCP tool response now includes:
- Main result/data
- Optional heartbeat footer showing:
  - Plan name, stage, directory
  - Last action taken
  - Stage-appropriate next action
  - Behavioral reminder to stay in plan mode

VERIFICATION:
- TypeScript build succeeded
- No compilation errors
- All 7 steps complete and tested", "type": "text"}]
